<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Lanschot cuts CSM to Underperformer.</title>
<headline>Van Lanschot cuts CSM to Underperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Research note summary (20/05)</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---------Broker---------</p>
<p>    CSM		 Foods	   104.50	  Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: Underperformer (from Market performer). Strong competition in food sector and dominant position of retailers has eroded CSM's operating margins and EPS growth. Although we expect PURAC to become the company's main EPS driver, we don't foresee double digit growth before 2000. Based on 97/98 P/E, stock is overvalued in comparison to the sector.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS    P/E    P/CF   Dividend   Op. margin</p>
<p>    1995/96 (actual)  5.17   20.22  13.79  1.70	 9.7</p>
<p>    1996/97	     5.55   18.81  12.32  1.90	 9.3</p>
<p>    1997/98	     6.00   17.43  11.19  2.00	 8.8</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
